  "notes": "Originally derived from the Chinese compass ({指南|しなん}{車|しゃ}), which points south — metaphorically meaning 'to show the correct direction.' The word has a classical, somewhat elevated tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {指南|しなん}する: to instruct, to coach\n- {指南|しなん}を{受|う}ける: to receive instruction\n- {指南|しなん}{役|やく}: instructor, coaching role\n- {指南|しなん}{書|しょ}: instruction manual, guidebook\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {指導|しどう}: guidance, leadership — the standard modern term for instruction; broader in scope\n- {教授|きょうじゅ}: teaching — formal instruction, especially academic\n- コーチング: coaching — modern loanword for coaching methodology\n- {師範|しはん}: master instructor — a title for someone qualified to teach traditional arts",
